    "reading-passage": {
      "nodeId": "542:5",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "📖 Reading Passage (B1)",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "📖 Reading Passage (B1)"
        },
        {
          "text": "Every morning starts in the bathroom. You turn on the faucet at the sink to wash your hands with hand soap and warm water. Then you squeeze toothpaste onto your toothbrush and brush your teeth for two minutes. After that, you might gargle with mouthwash to keep your breath fresh.\n\nNext, it is time for a shower. You step into the bathtub, pull the shower curtain closed, and adjust the shower head. You use shower gel or body wash to clean your body, and shampoo followed by conditioner for your hair. When you are finished, you dry off with a bath towel and step onto the bath mat.\n\nIn front of the mirror, you comb your hair with a comb or hairbrush. Many people apply lotion or face cream to keep their skin soft. Others use deodorant and sunscreen before getting dressed. The cabinet above the sink holds everyday items like dental floss, cotton swabs, a razor, and nail clippers.\n\nIt is important to keep the bathroom clean. A sponge and spray bottle help wipe down the tiles and sink. The laundry basket collects used towels and washcloths, and the plunger stays beside the toilet — just in case.",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Every morning starts in the bathroom. You turn on the faucet at the sink to wash your hands with hand soap and warm water. Then you squeeze toothpaste onto your toothbrush and brush your teeth for two minutes. After that, you might gargle with mouthwash to keep your breath fresh. Next, it is time for a shower. You step into the bathtub, pull the shower curtain closed, and adjust the shower head. You use shower gel or body wash to clean your body, and shampoo followed by conditioner for your hair. When you are finished, you dry off with a bath towel and step onto the bath mat. In front of the mirror, you comb your hair with a comb or hairbrush. Many people apply lotion or face cream to keep their skin soft. Others use deodorant and sunscreen before getting dressed. The cabinet above the sink holds everyday items like dental floss, cotton swabs, a razor, and nail clippers. It is important to keep the bathroom clean. A sponge and spray bottle help wipe down the tiles and sink. The laundry basket collects used towels and washcloths, and the plunger stays beside the toilet — just in case."
        },
        {
          "text": "Comprehension Questions",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Comprehension Questions"
        },
        {
          "text": "1.  What do you use to brush your teeth?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "1. What do you use to brush your teeth?"
        },
        {
          "text": "2.  What is the purpose of the shower curtain?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "2. What is the purpose of the shower curtain?"
        },
        {
          "text": "3.  Name three items you might find in the cabinet above the sink.",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "3. Name three items you might find in the cabinet above the sink."
        },
        {
          "text": "4.  How do you keep the bathroom clean according to the passage?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "4. How do you keep the bathroom clean according to the passage?"
        },
        {
          "text": "5.  What goes in the laundry basket?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "5. What goes in the laundry basket?"
        }
      ]
    },
    "idioms-phrases": {
      "nodeId": "542:17",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "💬 Idioms, Phrasal Verbs & Key Phrases",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "💬 Idioms, Phrasal Verbs & Key Phrases"
        },
        {
          "text": "throw in the towel",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "throw in the towel"
        },
        {
          "text": "(idiom) To give up. \"After three failed attempts, she threw in the towel.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "(idiom) To give up. \"After three failed attempts, she threw in the towel.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "clean up your act",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "clean up your act"
        },
        {
          "text": "(idiom) To improve your behavior. \"You need to clean up your act before the interview.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "(idiom) To improve your behavior. \"You need to clean up your act before the interview.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "come clean",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "come clean"
        },
        {
          "text": "(phrasal verb) To admit the truth. \"He finally came clean about breaking the vase.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "(phrasal verb) To admit the truth. \"He finally came clean about breaking the vase.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "wash your hands of",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "wash your hands of"
        },
        {
          "text": "(idiom) To refuse responsibility. \"She washed her hands of the whole project.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "(idiom) To refuse responsibility. \"She washed her hands of the whole project.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "down the drain",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "down the drain"
        },
        {
          "text": "(idiom) Wasted. \"All that hard work went down the drain.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "(idiom) Wasted. \"All that hard work went down the drain.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "scrub up well",
          "depth": 2,
